Z||000010||Will||03-31-2001||11:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B> Here's my theory. Progressive rate springs using coilovers I think would be benificial. Ride height aside, Say you adjusted so they fit snug.That would give you normal working rates. the tighter they were tensioned, the stiffer they would get.Solid rate springs would need to be changed whenever a different rate was desired.Of course this would be a seat of the pants type testing, but thats the only way I can do stuff. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What puts pressure on the springs? The weight of the car. Since your car isn't getting any heavier as you adjust your coil overs, you'd just be increasing your ride height, with no effect on spring rate.||||reg||1
